// bubbler profile: claude-code
//
// Claude Code installed the native way: `~/.local/bin/claude` is a
// symlink into `~/.local/share/claude/versions/`, and both are shared
// read-only, the link resolved on the host. Updating happens on the
// host; inside, DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER stops the attempt against a
// read-only tree. Installed from a package instead (`/usr/bin/claude`),
// drop both `home-share` nodes and write `command "claude"`.
//
// Create the instance once:
//     bubbler create claude-code --profile claude-code
// then, for every run, name the project and share it:
//     cd <project>
//     bubbler run claude-code --share .
// The share is for that run only, and the sandbox starts in it.
//
// The private home holds its own `~/.claude`: log in once inside
// (`/login`, copy the URL into a host browser, paste the code back), or
// copy `~/.claude/.credentials.json` into the instance home yourself.
// The host's `~/.claude` — history, settings, credentials — is never
// visible.
//
// Deliberately absent: an ssh agent, a keyring, the host's dotfiles, a
// display. `git` over SSH needs a key in the private home. The editor
// bridge (`/ide`) listens on the host's loopback and does not cross the
// network namespace.
//
// `userns "disable"`: bubbler is the boundary. Claude Code's own
// bubblewrap sandbox warns and is skipped; a Playwright or Chromium MCP
// server needs `userns "allow"` instead.
//
// Other switches, as `env` nodes: DISABLE_TELEMETRY="1",
// CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC="1".
//
// Stricter: `claude-code-strict` is this profile with the egress
// filtered by name — the tool reaches the hosts Anthropic documents as
// its network access requirements and nothing else, through a CONNECT
// proxy bubbler runs in the sandbox's network namespace. Create an
// instance from that profile, or replace the bare `network` node here
// with the whole block:
//
//     network {
//         outbound "deny"
//         allow-host "api.anthropic.com"
//         allow-host "claude.ai"
//         allow-host "platform.claude.com"
//         allow-host "downloads.claude.ai"
//         allow-host "registry.npmjs.org"
//         allow-host "raw.githubusercontent.com"
//         allow-host "browser-intake-us5-datadoghq.com"
//         allow-host "http-intake.logs.us5.datadoghq.com"
//     }
//     lint-allow "outbound-deny" reason="egress is filtered by name here, not by address"
//
// `WebFetch` of a URL off that list, a plugin marketplace hosted
// anywhere but GitHub's raw host, and an MCP server reaching a service
// of its own all stop working; each is one more `allow-host` line. The
// application gets no DNS of its own under it, and the run needs a
// delegated cgroup2 subtree (a systemd user session has one) beside the
// `passt` and `nftables` packages.
network
userns "disable"
env DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER="1"
home-share ".local/bin/claude" mode=ro
home-share ".local/share/claude" mode=ro
command "/home/bubbler/.local/bin/claude"
